            ),
        ],
        description: "CMake: Set the extension base directory to the duckdb module dir\n\nDuckDB\'s extension-patch step hardcodes `${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}`, which only equals the\nsubmodule root in a standalone build. When DuckDB is pulled in via `add_subdirectory`,\nit resolves to the parent project\'s root, which causes the patch script and patch-dir\nlookups to happen in the wrong place.\n\nI ran into this because I\'m vendoring duckDB as a submodule for a Python bindings project,\nand statically link extensions from the submodule checkout in the build process.\n",
    },
)
